---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

// Text ported from the published app policy at
// sudo-acraciun.github.io/movienight/privacy-policy.html, with the two
// self-referencing links pointing at this site. It also carries a "Website
// analytics" section that the app copy does not: this site runs PostHog
// (cookieless) while the app does not, so the two policies deliberately
// diverge on that one point. The date is bumped for that added disclosure.
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | I Like Movies"
  description="What I Like Movies collects, why, who processes it, and how to access, export or delete your data."
  path="/privacy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="16 August 2026"
>
  <p>
    I Like Movies (the "app") is a movie-tracking and recommendation app operated by Alexandru
    Crăciun, based in the Netherlands ("we", "us"). This policy explains what we collect, why, and
    the choices you have. It applies to everyone who uses the app, anywhere in the world.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account details</strong> — your name and email address from Google Sign-In. Used to
      create and identify your account. We never receive your Google password.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Things you create in the app</strong> — your ratings, reviews, notes, lists,
      watchlist, friend connections, household membership, and the messages you send to the in-app
      assistant (including their text and any image you choose to attach). Stored so the app can
      show them back to you and your friends.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Photos you add</strong> — a profile photo, and any image you attach to an assistant
      chat. Stored on our server.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your country</strong> — the country you set, used to show which streaming services
      carry a title where you are.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Notification token</strong> — a device push token, used only to deliver the
      notifications you enable.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Voice messages</strong> — when you dictate a message, your phone transcribes the
      speech using your device's speech service and the app receives only the resulting <em>text</em
      >. We do not record or store your audio.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data</strong> — your IP address and basic request logs, used to keep the
      service running, secure, and free of abuse.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> access your phone's contacts, and we do not collect location beyond
    the country you choose.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal bases (EU/UK GDPR)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>To provide the app</strong> — performance of our agreement with you.</li>
    <li><strong>To keep it secure and prevent abuse</strong> — our legitimate interests.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Notifications and other optional features</strong> — your consent, which you can
      withdraw at any time.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
  <p>
    We use a small number of trusted service providers to run the app and this website. We do not
    sell your data or use it for advertising.
  </p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <tr><th>Provider</th><th>What it handles</th></tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Google (Sign-In)</td>
        <td>Verifies your identity and gives us your name and email.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>The Movie Database (TMDB) &amp; OMDb</td>
        <td>
          Movie and TV metadata. We send title queries and your country to look up details and
          streaming availability.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Anthropic (Claude)</td>
        <td>
          Powers the in-app assistant. The text (and any image) you send to the assistant is
          processed to generate a reply.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Render</td>
        <td>Hosts our application and database in the European Union (Frankfurt).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr><td>Expo</td><td>Delivers push notifications to your device.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sentry</td><td>Collects crash and error diagnostics so we can fix problems.</td></tr>
      <tr>
        <td>PostHog</td>
        <td>
          Cookieless analytics for this website (ilikemovies.app) only: visit counts and where
          visitors arrived from, processed in the European Union.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Your data is stored in the European Union. Some of our providers (for example Google, Anthropic,
    Sentry and Expo) are based in the United States, so providing the app may involve transferring
    some data there. Where that happens, we rely on those providers' standard data-protection
    safeguards.
  </p>

  <h2>Website analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This website (ilikemovies.app), as distinct from the app, uses PostHog to understand how many
    people visit, where they arrived from, and whether they tap through to Google Play. It runs
    without cookies: it stores nothing on your device, does not track you across other sites, and
    does not build a profile that identifies you. We do not use any of it for advertising and we do
    not sell it. PostHog processes this for us in the European Union (Frankfurt) under a
    data-processing agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your data for as long as your account exists. When you delete your account, we
    permanently erase your account and the data tied to it. Residual copies in encrypted backups are
    removed on the normal backup rotation (within 30 days).
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can access, correct, export, or delete your data, and object to or restrict certain
    processing. If you're in the EU/EEA or UK, these are your GDPR rights; if you're in California,
    we confirm we do not sell or share your personal information. To exercise any right, use the
    in-app controls or email us (below).
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your account and data</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your account at any time from <strong>Settings → Delete Account</strong> in the
    app — this permanently erases your account and associated data immediately. If you can't sign
    in, you can request deletion at our <a href="/delete-account">account-deletion page</a> or by
    emailing us.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The app is not directed to children under 16, and we don't knowingly collect their data.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Traffic is encrypted in transit (HTTPS). Access to our systems is restricted, and the assistant
    has no ability to act outside the app on your behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We'll update this page if our practices change and revise the date at the top.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:ilikemovies.review@gmail.com"
      >ilikemovies.review@gmail.com</a
    >.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
